    "notationFootnote": "",
    "author": "Jan Braunstein",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Chromatic Lyre Notation (Jan Braunstein, 2009). Major-third 2-line staff at E/G# with a C ledger; binary-6-6 fill INVERTED relative to Clairnote/Beyreuther — the line-side whole-tone set {C,D,E,F#,G#,A#} hollow, the other set solid (per the operator reference; designed so handwritten solid dots don't blend into lines). The traditional alto clef with incorporated 8va/8vb/15va/15vb register variants (E1) is exercised here in register-label (text) clef mode showing 'C' (the alto clef marks middle C); the published alto-clef glyph shape is deferred as an asset. The duration devices (stemless half notes; whole/double-whole side lines) are notehead-baked marks the platform can express but are not built into this single-duration preview — documented. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
